<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  XForge's entitlements.

  These are the only ones the app asks for, and they are here on purpose:

  * com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing — the compiler runs in
    this process, and LLVM maps large regions: the SDK's symbol tables, the object
    files the linker reads back, and the JIT's reserved code space. The entitlement
    was originally needed by the embedded Linux guest that used to live in this
    process; the guest is gone, and no measurement has been taken since, so it is
    kept for the compiler's maps rather than removed on a guess.

  * com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit — a compiler's working set is
    large (LLVM and Swift's frontend are linked into the app, and a build holds a
    module graph in memory). The default jetsam budget is below what a real compile
    needs, so this asks for the larger limit.

  Both are also the keys a signer may refuse: a wildcard or free-account profile
  cannot always grant them. If a sideloader strips them, XForge still installs and
  runs — it gets the default address space and memory budget, which is enough for
  small projects and not for large ones.

  * get-task-allow — true, which is what a development-signed app has; a
    sideloader re-signs with its own certificate and sets this itself.

  * application-identifier — the signing identity. The $(AppIdentifierPrefix)
    placeholder is resolved by the signer from its provisioning profile, so it
    must not be hardcoded here.

  Deliberately absent: keychain-access-groups, app groups, user-fonts,
  notifications, network extensions. The app uses none of them, and asking for
  an entitlement a free-account profile cannot grant makes some sideloaders
  refuse the install outright — the safe set is the set that is actually used.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>get-task-allow</key>
	<true/>
	<key>application-identifier</key>
	<string>$(AppIdentifierPrefix)$(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER)</string>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.extended-virtual-addressing</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
